WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.588
What does this prove federally?

2
00:00:01.588 --> 00:00:06.884
That every issuing CA is trusted with
a CRL Entra can download in time,

3
00:00:06.884 --> 00:00:11.345
which supports acceptance of
PIV credentials and public

4
00:00:11.345 --> 00:00:15.062
key-based authentication,
IA-2 twelve and IA-5 two.

5
00:00:15.062 --> 00:00:20.206
That an enabled policy requires a
phishing-resistant strength and PIV counts as

6
00:00:20.206 --> 00:00:23.278
multifactor, which the
SCuBA baseline requires;

7
00:00:23.278 --> 00:00:26.349
keep those two rows beside
the ScubaGear report.

8
00:00:26.349 --> 00:00:32.150
That a revoked card is refused, which
is FIPS 201's termination of the card.

9
00:00:32.150 --> 00:00:35.090
And that the certificate counts
at the assurance claimed.
